From: ZhengShaobo <zhengshaobo1@xiaomi.com>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: gov_power_allocator: grant max power when idle

When no cooling actor requests power, setting total_req_power to 1 still
grants every actor zero power.  CPUFreq and devfreq cooling then interpret
that as maximum cooling, even when the device is idle.  Grant each actor
its maximum power in this case.

Backport of upstream commit 08eb0493f6b3583b2efc90665a3e6980faee56a0.

---
 drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c b/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c
index 1b2345a697c5..4301516c0938 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c
@@ -354,10 +354,18 @@ static void divvy_up_power(struct power_actor *power, int num_actors,
 	int i;
 
 	/*
-	 * Prevent division by 0 if none of the actors request power.
+	 * Nobody requested anything, just give everybody
+	 * the maximum power
 	 */
-	if (!total_req_power)
-		total_req_power = 1;
+	if (!total_req_power) {
+		for (i = 0; i < num_actors; i++) {
+			struct power_actor *pa = &power[i];
+
+			pa->granted_power = pa->max_power;
+		}
+
+		return;
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < num_actors; i++) {
 		struct power_actor *pa = &power[i];
